  "caption": "Quinn's pre-gym plan was coffee, then more coffee. By cup four, Quinn was buzzing until 11pm.\n\nCaffeine can give a real but modest boost, mostly by making effort feel a bit easier. More is not better, and dropping off quickly doesn't mean your sleep wasn't affected.\n\nWhat often helps: saving it for sessions where a small edge matters, having it early enough to protect sleep (roughly nine hours before bed for a coffee-sized dose), checking pre-workout labels, staying within general adult guidance of about 400 mg a day, and taking the odd break so it keeps its kick.\n\nPalpitations, tremor, anxiety or poor sleep are signs to cut back. If you have heart rhythm or blood pressure concerns, talk to your GP first.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
